.TH PLANSPLEASE 1 "October 2026" "plansplease" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
plansplease \- publish and upload immutable HTML snapshots
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B plansplease
.RI [ global-options ]
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B plansplease help
[\fIcommand\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B plansplease
uses the existing local profiles, documents, credentials, and daemon.
The npm package, local data paths, and PLANVIEW environment settings retain their existing names.
.PP
.B plansplease
publishes an HTML file or page folder to a local daemon and returns a stable
localhost URL. It can also upload an HTML file or artifact folder to the cloud workspace.
A page folder must contain
.B index.html
and is published with its assets.
.PP
Use
.B --profile name
before the command to use an isolated set of documents and daemon state.
The default profile keeps the existing Planview data directory. Named profiles
are stored below
.B planview/profiles/name
.
.PP
The
.B publish
command creates a snapshot and prints its URL. Pass
.B \-\-open
to open the URL in the default browser after publishing.
.PP
Use
.B login
before
.B upload
to authorize this computer in a browser. Cloud preview links require the same
account to be signed in in the browser.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B publish [options] file|folder
Publish an immutable HTML snapshot and print its URL. Use
.B \-\-open
to open the URL in the default browser.
.TP
.B login [options]
Open the selected app's account sign-in in a browser and authorize this computer.
Hosted apps use GitHub sign-in; the local workspace uses its local test account. Use
.B \-\-cloud-url origin
to sign in to another app origin.
.TP
.B logout
Revoke the saved cloud sign-in on the app, then remove it from this computer.
Revocation requires a connection.
.TP
.B upload [options] file.html|folder
Upload an HTML file or artifact folder and print its workspace preview URL. Folders require index.html, at most 512 files, and 8 MiB including the manifest.
The preview requires an authenticated browser session.
.TP
.B get id|url
Write a stored snapshot's exact bytes to standard output. The reference must be
a document id or an exact local preview URL.
.TP
.B start [options]
Start the local daemon, or reuse the authenticated daemon already running.
.TP
.B status [options]
Show daemon status without starting a daemon.
.TP
.B stop [options]
Gracefully stop the local daemon.
.TP
.B restart [options]
Restart the local daemon.
.TP
.B clean [options]
Remove expired snapshots and reconcile incomplete storage operations.
.TP
.B list [--limit 1..100] [--after id] [--json]
List an ID-ordered page of local snapshots, including immutable generations and
expiry timestamps, without extending retention. Default limit is 50.
.TP
.B usage [--json]
Show committed document bytes plus 4 KiB metadata per snapshot, the 1 GiB quota,
and 30-day last-access retention. This is logical storage, not physical disk use.
.TP
.B delete id --generation value [--json]
Delete a selected local snapshot generation from list. Active reads retain it;
stale generations cannot delete replacements. Cloud copies are independent.
Partial failures require clean for bounded reconciliation, possibly after the
orphan recovery grace period. Deletion exits 1 for stale, retained or partial;
missing metadata returns not_found and exit 0 without claiming residual files are gone.
.TP
.B ui [--open] [--json]
Start an optional browser manager in the existing daemon and print a private,
one-use launch link. Browser opening is explicit with --open. The manager has
a distinct loopback origin and independent in-memory browser sessions. It lists,
opens, copies, deletes selected generations, shows storage/retention, and imports
standalone HTML up to 10 MiB. Launch codes expire after one minute; sessions last
up to eight hours. Reloading needs a fresh link. Stop daemon & previews or
plansplease stop shuts down both listeners. No cloud action occurs.
.TP
.B help [command]
Show help for the whole CLI or for one command.
.SH AGENT SKILLS
Install Planview's skills with the Vercel Skills CLI from a project directory:
.EX
npx skills add https://github.com/abijith-suresh/plansplease/tree/main/apps/cli/skills
.EE
From a Planview checkout, use
.B npx skills add ./apps/cli/skills
instead. Skills CLI installs to the project by default; use
.B \-g
for optional user-wide installation. Use
.B \-a codex \-y
for a non-interactive Codex install.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show the relevant help text. Use
.B plansplease help command
to request help explicitly.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Show the plansplease CLI version.
.TP
.B \-\-profile name
Use the named profile for this invocation. Names start with a lowercase letter
or number and contain only lowercase letters, numbers, hyphens, and underscores.
.TP
.B \-\-open
Open the returned URL in the default browser. Supported by
.B publish
and
.B upload
and
.B ui
.
.TP
.B \-\-cloud-url origin
Select the cloud app origin for
.B login
.
.TP
.B PLANVIEW_CLOUD_URL
Environment variable selecting the default cloud app origin for
.B login
.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print one newline-terminated JSON object for metadata commands. Supported by
.B publish
,
.B start
,
.B status
,
.B stop
,
.B restart
,
and
.B clean
,
.B upload
,
.B list
,
.B usage
, and
.B delete
, and
.B ui
.
.TP
.B \-\-
Stop option parsing. Text after this marker is treated as an operand.
.SH OUTPUT
Successful text output goes to standard output. Errors go to standard error.
.B get
writes only the stored document bytes to standard output.
.PP
With
.B \-\-json
, successful metadata commands write one JSON object followed by a newline.
JSON errors use an
.B error
object on standard error. The
.B get
command does not accept
.B \-\-json
because its output is the stored document itself.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.local/share/planview
Default application data directory on supported Unix systems.
.TP
.B ~/.local/share/planview/profiles/name
Application data directory for a named profile on supported Unix systems.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
The command could not complete, or its arguments were invalid.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
plansplease publish ./report.html
plansplease publish --open ./site
plansplease login --cloud-url http://127.0.0.1:3000
plansplease upload ./report.html
plansplease logout
plansplease get http://localhost:4777/<id> > report.html
plansplease status --json
plansplease publish --json ./report.html
plansplease help publish
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR npm (1),
.BR man (1)

.SH SHARING A LOCAL SNAPSHOT
.B plansplease share [--json] [--open] LOCAL_ID
uploads the existing daemon-owned immutable bytes with a durable account/origin
operation key. Publish remains local-only; legacy upload remains explicit.
Unknown operations recover by authenticated receipt lookup without resending bytes.
Use --operation KEY to select an existing attempt, or --inspect for bounded local
metadata without cloud work. Only terminal failure permits deliberate --new-attempt.
Never replace an unknown key. Exit 0 means cloud committed and receipt recorded;
exit 1 means failed, unknown, or local bookkeeping uncertain. JSON separates local,
cloud, bookkeeping and recovery. Cloud refusal preserves local data, including
local 10 MiB snapshots above the cloud 8 MiB limit. Local/cloud deletion is
independent. Sharing does not pin or extend 30-day/1 GiB local retention.

.SH BUILD IDENTITY
.B build-info [--json]
prints the installed version and candidate source SHA/channel as bounded JSON,
without starting a daemon or reading cloud credentials. Regular packages report
build: null. Candidates require the pinned Node/npm runtime and a prepared npm
cache for external Effect 4.0.6; their tarball is not self-contained.
.PP
A candidate refuses to reuse a selected profile daemon from another build.
Inspect status, then explicitly stop that owned profile before starting the new
candidate. Stopping ends both preview and manager listeners and old preview
links. Other profiles remain independent. Candidate preparation does not publish
or move npm tags.
